From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake/physx5: add riscv64 library path

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riseproject.dev builds PhysX from source for riscv64 rather than fetching a precompiled archive]

cmake/physx5.cmake only fetches a precompiled PhysX archive; there is
no riscv64 archive (sapien-sim/physx-precompiled publishes macOS,
linux-aarch64, linux x86_64 and windows only). We build PhysX from
source instead and point SAPIEN_PHYSX5_DIR at the install tree, which
this file already supports via `IS_DIRECTORY ${SAPIEN_PHYSX5_DIR}` --
skipping the FetchContent branch entirely. What's missing is the
arch-selection block below it that picks which `bin/linux.<arch>/...`
subdirectory to link against: riscv64 would silently fall into the
x86_64-labeled `bin/linux.clang/release` bucket (the plain ELSE()).
Give it its own `bin/linux.riscv64/release` bucket instead, and make
our from-source PhysX build (build-sapien.yml) install into that
exact path.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 cmake/physx5.cmake | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cmake/physx5.cmake b/cmake/physx5.cmake
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/cmake/physx5.cmake
+++ b/cmake/physx5.cmake
@@ -68,6 +68,8 @@ elseif(UNIX)

   if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "aarch64|arm64")
     target_link_directories(physx5 INTERFACE $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${physx5_SOURCE_DIR}/bin/linux.aarch64/release>)
+  elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "riscv64")
+    target_link_directories(physx5 INTERFACE $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${physx5_SOURCE_DIR}/bin/linux.riscv64/release>)
   else()
     if (CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE STREQUAL "Debug")
       target_link_directories(physx5 INTERFACE $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${physx5_SOURCE_DIR}/bin/linux.clang/checked>)
--
